+0623. Intel 8080-compatible binary execution baseline
+
+      A generic CP/M 2.2 binary personality shall execute documented
+      Intel 8080 instructions with their documented register, flag,
+      stack, control-flow, and encoding semantics sufficiently to run
+      the CP/M environment and 8080 transient programs.
+
+      Disposition: REQUIRED
+
+      Evidence:    I063 PROCESSOR INSTRUCTION PROFILE subsystem IG AG;
+                   sections 4-6 and T01-T03; I064; I067.
+
+      Conformance: Run an 8080-only instruction/flag probe and
+                   representative CP/M software on the claimed
+                   execution environment.
+
+
+0624. Declared processor-profile instruction semantics
+
+      A configuration advertising a processor profile shall implement
+      the documented instructions and CPU-visible state of that profile
+      while preserving every generic CP/M requirement it inherits. A
+      Z80 claim includes its documented extensions and 8080-compatible
+      subset; a processor profile may add but may not waive requirements.
+
+      Disposition: REQUIRED
+
+      Evidence:    I063 PROCESSOR INSTRUCTION PROFILE subsystem IG AG;
+                   T03-T05; I064; I067 HARDWARE PROFILE VALIDATION
+                   subsystem IG AG.
+
+      Conformance: Test profile-specific instruction families separately
+                   from CP/M service tests, then run the inherited
+                   generic CP/M suite unchanged.
+
+
+0625. Z80 extensions outside a generic CP/M claim
+
+      Documented Z80-only instructions and registers are not required by
+      a generic CP/M 2.2 claim that does not advertise a Z80 processor
+      profile.
+
+      Disposition: NOT REQUIRED
+
+      Evidence:    I063 PROCESSOR INSTRUCTION PROFILE subsystem IG AG;
+                   DRI source screen and T01-T05; I067.
+
+      Conformance: Do not fail a generic 8080-profile implementation
+                   merely because a Z80-only transient cannot execute.
+
+
+0626. Undocumented processor behavior
+
+      Undocumented opcodes, undocumented flag bits, and results of
+      instructions outside the selected processor profile are not
+      guaranteed by generic CP/M 2.2.
+
+      Disposition: NOT GUARANTEED
+
+      Evidence:    I063 PROCESSOR INSTRUCTION PROFILE subsystem IG AG;
+                   T06-T07; I067.
+
+      Conformance: A generic suite may verify permitted variation or
+                   trapping; stronger behavior requires a named profile.
+
+
+0627. Processor timing and interrupt topology
+
+      CP/M 2.2 does not require a universal CPU clock, exact instruction
+      timing, wait-state pattern, refresh behavior, or machine interrupt
+      topology.
+
+      Disposition: NOT REQUIRED
+
+      Evidence:    I063 PROCESSOR INSTRUCTION PROFILE subsystem IG AG;
+                   section 7 and T08; I051; I065; I067.
+
+      Conformance: Test such properties only under a profile that
+                   explicitly advertises them.
+
